---
import ArrowIcon from '../../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/site.css';
import '../../styles/pablomi.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pablomi — social and messaging app" description="Explore Pablomi, Noah Adofina’s independently designed and developed desktop-first social and messaging app for gamers, preparing for private testing.">
  <main id="main" class="case-study">
    <section class="case-hero" aria-labelledby="case-title">
      <div class="case-top micro"><a href="/work"><ArrowIcon direction="left" /> BACK TO WORK</a><span>CURRENT PROJECT / IN DEVELOPMENT</span></div>
      <div class="case-title-grid">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT BUILD / DESKTOP FIRST</p><h1 id="case-title">PABLOMI<span>.</span></h1></div>
        <div class="case-lede"><p>A social and messaging app for gamers, designed around the ways friends stay connected while they play.</p><span class="status-pill">PREPARING FOR PRIVATE TESTING</span><a class="case-site-link" href="https://pablomi.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit Pablomi website <ArrowIcon direction="up-right" /></a></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="case-lead-shot"><a href="/projects/full/chat.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-chat" data-lightbox-alt="Current Pablomi chat screen with friends sidebar, messages, shared media, and composer." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi chat / current development build" aria-label="View full Pablomi chat screenshot"><img src="/projects/pablomi-chat.webp" alt="Pablomi chat screen with a friends sidebar, conversation, shared media, and message composer." width="1913" height="1079" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption class="micro">CHAT / CURRENT DEVELOPMENT BUILD · SELECT TO VIEW FULL SCREENSHOT</figcaption></figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-intro" aria-labelledby="case-intro-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE EXPERIENCE</p>
      <div><h2 id="case-intro-title">FRIENDS, CHAT,<br /><span class="serif">one place.</span></h2><p>Pablomi brings direct and group conversations, friends, profiles, themes, and voice into a desktop-first interface. Accounts can be customized, and the app includes notifications, unread counts, and controls for managing friendships and groups.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-sequence" aria-labelledby="showcase-title">
      <div class="feature-heading"><p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT SHOWCASE</p><h2 id="showcase-title">AROUND THE <span class="serif">conversation.</span></h2><p>These screens are from the current development build. Open any image to see the full interface.</p></div>
      <article class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-text"><span class="micro">01 / FRIENDS</span><h3>YOUR PEOPLE.</h3><p>The friends view keeps profiles in the main area while conversations remain close in the sidebar.</p><a href="/projects/full/friends.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-friends" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi friends view with profile cards and a persistent sidebar." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi friends / current development build">View full screenshot</a></div>
        <figure class="feature-crop-top"><a href="/projects/full/friends.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-friends" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi friends view with profile cards and a persistent sidebar." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi friends / current development build" aria-label="View full Pablomi friends screenshot"><img src="/projects/pablomi-friends.webp" alt="Pablomi friends view with profile cards and a messaging sidebar." width="1919" height="1079" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>FRIENDS / CURRENT PABLOMI</figcaption></figure>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-row feature-row-reverse">
        <div class="feature-text"><span class="micro">02 / PROFILES</span><h3>MAKE IT YOURS.</h3><p>Profiles bring together identity details, social links, and a personal background.</p><a href="/projects/full/profile.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-profile" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi profile with a personal background and social links." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi profile / current development build">View full screenshot</a></div>
        <figure><a href="/projects/full/profile.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-profile" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi profile with a personal background and social links." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi profile / current development build" aria-label="View full Pablomi profile screenshot"><img src="/projects/pablomi-profile.webp" alt="Pablomi profile with identity details, social links, and a personalized background." width="1910" height="1079" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>PROFILE / CURRENT PABLOMI</figcaption></figure>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-text"><span class="micro">03 / THEMES</span><h3>CHANGE THE LOOK.</h3><p>The settings screen includes a gallery for browsing and choosing interface themes.</p><a href="/projects/full/themes.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-themes" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi settings with theme previews, search, and color filters." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi themes / current development build">View full screenshot</a></div>
        <figure><a href="/projects/full/themes.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-themes" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi settings with theme previews, search, and color filters." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi themes / current development build" aria-label="View full Pablomi themes screenshot"><img src="/projects/pablomi-themes.webp" alt="Pablomi settings with a theme gallery, search, and color filters." width="1917" height="1079" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>THEMES / CURRENT PABLOMI</figcaption></figure>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-row feature-row-reverse">
        <div class="feature-text"><span class="micro">04 / VOICE</span><h3>TALK WHILE YOU PLAY.</h3><p>Voice controls sit alongside the message thread, keeping voice and text in the same space.</p><a href="/projects/full/voice.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-voice" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi chat view with voice controls in the sidebar." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi voice / current development build">View full screenshot</a></div>
        <figure><a href="/projects/full/voice.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-case" data-lightbox-id="case-voice" data-lightbox-alt="Pablomi chat view with voice controls in the sidebar." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi voice / current development build" aria-label="View full Pablomi voice screenshot"><img src="/projects/pablomi-voice.webp" alt="Pablomi chat view showing voice controls beside the message thread." width="1919" height="1079" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>VOICE / CURRENT PABLOMI</figcaption></figure>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="case-engineering" aria-labelledby="engineering-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE PRODUCT</p><h2 id="engineering-title">BUILT<br /><span class="serif">independently.</span></h2></div>
      <div class="engineering-copy"><p>I designed and developed Pablomi across the client, desktop shell, API, data model, and moderation tools. The desktop app uses Tauri 2 and Rust with a React, JavaScript, and Vite frontend. A Node.js and Express backend uses PostgreSQL, Firebase Authentication, Socket.io and WebSockets for realtime communication, and WebRTC for voice. A separate React application supports administration and moderation.</p><p>I completed the migration from Electron to Tauri 2 while preserving the existing React app and moving its native desktop integrations. Tauri is now the supported Windows desktop shell.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="case-systems" aria-labelledby="systems-title">
      <div class="systems-heading"><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING HIGHLIGHTS</p><h2 id="systems-title">WHAT WENT INTO <span class="serif">the build.</span></h2></div>
      <div class="systems-grid">
        <article><h3>Messaging and presence</h3><p>I built persistent direct and group messaging with live delivery, presence, reactions, editing, deletion, membership, and invitations. Reconnect recovery helps clients catch up after a disconnect.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Accounts and safety</h3><p>Authentication, authorization, account security, sessions, device management, and remote revocation are part of the system. I also built separate moderation and safety tooling.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Testing and reliability</h3><p>Automated integration and regression tests cover core server and realtime paths. I’m continuing live multi-session, deployment, and installed-build verification before private testing.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evolution" aria-labelledby="evolution-title">
      <div class="evolution-heading"><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT EVOLUTION</p><h2 id="evolution-title">FROM CHECKPOINT<br /><span class="serif">to Pablomi.</span></h2><p>The project began under the Checkpoint name. These profile screens show how its layout and visual identity changed over time.</p></div>
      <div class="evolution-images">
        <figure><a href="/projects/full/Checkpoint Main.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-evolution" data-lightbox-id="evolution-checkpoint" data-lightbox-alt="Older Checkpoint profile screen with its previous name and layout." data-lightbox-caption="Checkpoint / earlier profile view" aria-label="View full earlier Checkpoint profile screenshot"><img src="/projects/checkpoint-profile.webp" alt="Older Checkpoint profile screen, showing the previous name and layout." width="1385" height="850" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>EARLIER BUILD / CHECKPOINT</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><a href="/projects/full/profile.png" data-lightbox data-gallery="pablomi-evolution" data-lightbox-id="evolution-pablomi" data-lightbox-alt="Current Pablomi profile with personal background and social links." data-lightbox-caption="Pablomi / current profile view" aria-label="View full current Pablomi profile screenshot"><img src="/projects/pablomi-profile.webp" alt="Current Pablomi profile with identity details, social links, and a personalized background." width="1910" height="1079" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>CURRENT BUILD / PABLOMI</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-close"><p class="eyebrow">CURRENT STATUS</p><h2>PREPARING FOR<br /><span class="serif">private testing.</span></h2><p>Pablomi is functional and actively developed. I’m working through live multi-session acceptance, deployment and installed-build verification, reliability improvements, a controlled rollout of application-session enforcement, and release preparation.</p><div class="case-close-links"><a class="button-green" href="/work">Back to all projects</a><a class="text-link" href="https://pablomi.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit Pablomi website</a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
